I verified the recalled same-value RowsAffected claim on the web: SQLite counts matched rows. Sources: https://stackoverflow.com/questions/26372449/sqlite-changes-counts-non-changing-updates and https://dotclear.placeoweb.com/post/SQL-matching-found-rows-vs-affected-rows ('client SQLite : "found (matched) rows" uniquement'). So the COALESCE repeat answers 303.

The CrossOriginProtection and details claims are consistent with known behaviour and their if_wrong fallbacks are harmless.

These code claims hold in the tree:
- visibleSQL (comments.go:62);
- treeSQL filters only on report_id (tree.go:55);
- arrange's keep rule (tree.go:124);
- adminReport never reads the tree (admin.go:119-151);
- threadOf and buildLevel signatures;
- TestReaderPagesShareOneLayout covers owner and non-owner (reader_test.go:233);
- observe() has POST /admin/feedback/1/reply (vote_test.go:534).

Two stale rationale lines change nothing in the spec:
- 'with Q-012 open there is no JavaScript': static/thread.js already ships under script-src 'self' (router.go:110-113, report.html:5).
- 'every existing handler answers 400 to a ... unknown field': unknown fields are ignored (comment.go:68-80). The planned handler checks only `from`, which matches the code.

Finding m2: the E-006 case's literal message was never measured.

Checked:
- a reply racing a removal (refused inside Post's single statement);
- the report deleted between RemoveTarget and Remove (0 rows, 404);
- draft and unpublished reports (admin landing);
- all comments removed ('0 comments' plus 'No comments yet.');
- `from` given in the query string (ignored by PostForm);
- a POST with no Content-Type (ParseForm returns nil).

Gaps filed: m4 (branch-page landing) and m5 (no UI removes a blocked writer's comment).

m6: 'removed' wording for a placeholder parent that may only be blocked.

Otherwise the contracts match the code they extend:
- adminFeedbackReply's target-first order;
- canonicalID's 404 for the access matrix's 'x';
- ownerRouteStatus' 404 for own-method and 405 for other-method rows (admin_test.go:82-101);
- the auth.SeeOther landings built from the stored slug.
